{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Who heals the brokenhearted</b> — they are the mourners of Zion." "<b>And binds up</b> — like: לא זרו ולא חבשו (they were not winnowed and not bound). R. Isaac the Sephardi said: it is like לעצבותם, like the language of Ishmael, and similar to it: ידיך עצבוני. And in my opinion: it is like נגעם, for the one who touches a great nerve suffers on their account."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 147, :notes {1 "R. Isaac interprets ומחבש as related to עצבות (sorrow), citing Arabic; Ibn Ezra rejects this and reads it as related to נגע/עצב (wound, nerve)."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:59.636046101Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}